      "title": "Beau Lamarre-Condon trial: prosecution begins cross-examination of double murder accused – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/nov/06/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-former-police-accused-murder-case-jesse-baird-luke-davies-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>This blog has now closed</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/06/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-witness-box-evidence-case-ntwnfb\">Beau Lamarre-Condon tells double murder trial shooting of Jesse Baird wasn’t intentional but ‘it was my fault’</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Lamarre-Condon tells the court he had seen what he assumed to be someone’s delivery motorcycle:</p><p><em>As soon as I saw that I had an idea … I saw a hi-vis hooded jacket, waterproof long pants and gloves.</em></p><p><em>This moment here … I wish that I didn’t do this … But I had the thought process that if I was to put on this helmet and outfit I could knock on Jesse’s door I would look like an UberEats driver without any verbal interaction with Jesse.</em></p><p>At the very least I would have had an AVO out against me … police don’t hesitate to put another police on an AVO … I was worried if I knocked on the door it would be perceived as harassment.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/nov/06/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-former-police-accused-murder-case-jesse-baird-luke-davies-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-06T02:30:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Liberal bus crashes into shop awning on its first outing of Victorian election campaign",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/06/liberal-jess-wilson-campaign-bus-crashes-into-shop-first-day-victorian-election",
      "description": "<p>Opposition leader Jess Wilson grimaced as the ‘Jess Express’, carrying Liberals and reporters, backs into the structure in suburban Melbourne</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Victorian Liberal party’s first offical day on the campaign trail has hit a snag, after its campaign bus reversed into the awning of a shopfront.</p><p>The “Jess Express”, a large blue bus emblazoned with an image of the opposition leader, Jess Wilson, was unveiled on Friday, 12 days after Labor launched its own red equivalent.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/06/liberal-jess-wilson-campaign-bus-crashes-into-shop-first-day-victorian-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
