    {
      "title": "Beau Lamarre-Condon tells double murder trial shooting of Jesse Baird wasn’t intentional but ‘it was my fault’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/06/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-witness-box-evidence-case-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Former NSW police officer gives evidence for a second day after pleading not guilty to murdering Baird and Luke Davies in early 2024</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/nov/06/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-former-police-accused-murder-case-jesse-baird-luke-davies-ntwnfb\">Beau Lamarre-Condon trial live updates: former police officer continues evidence in double murder trial</a></p></li></ul><p>Beau Lamarre-Condon has said he is “guilty of manslaughter” but said shooting Jesse Baird wasn’t intentional, as he gave evidence in his double-murder trial.</p><p>The former police officer is accused of fatally shooting Baird and his partner, Luke Davies, with his police service weapon in Baird’s Paddington home in Sydney on 19 February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/06/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-witness-box-evidence-case-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-06T01:36:20"
    }
